    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0962" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg838"/>

                <head>No. 507.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Señor de
                        Zamacona.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 26,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 18th instant accompanied by an extract from the El Paso
                    Times, of the 8th of the present month, relative to certain United States
                    reservation Indians who have committed depredations and murder in Mexico, while
                    on leave of absence.</p>
                <p>I have communicated a copy of your note and of its accompaniment to the Secretary
                    of the Interior for his information and for such action as he may properly cause
                    to be taken in the matter.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
